Below is a minimal example of a “rotating card” that flips when you hover over it.  
It uses only **HTML** and **CSS** (no JavaScript).  

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* ---------- Container ----------
   Keeps the perspective so the flip looks 3‑D */
.card-wrapper {
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    margin: 50px auto;          /* center horizontally */
    perspective: 1000px;        /* depth of the 3‑D space */
}

/* ---------- Card ----------
   Two sides stacked on top of each other */
.card {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    position: relative;
    transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* allow children to be positioned in 3‑D */
    transition: transform 0.6s ease;/* smooth rotation */
}

.card:hover {                     /* rotate when hovered */
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* ---------- Front & Back ----------
   Both occupy the same space, but back is rotated 180° */
.front,
.back {
    position: absolute;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    backface-visibility: hidden;   /* hide backside when facing away */
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

.front {
    background: #fff;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: #333;
}

.back {
    background: #3498db;
    color: #fff;
    transform: rotateY(180deg);     /* start flipped */
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front side -->
        <div class="front">
            <p>Front Side</p>
        </div>
        <!-- Back side -->
        <div class="back">
            <p>Back Side</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Provides a 3‑D perspective (`perspective: 1000px`). |
| `.card` | Holds both sides; `transform-style: preserve-3d` allows its children to be positioned in 3‑D. |
| `.card:hover` | Rotates the whole card 180° around the Y‑axis. |
| `.front`, `.back` | Each occupies the same space; `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the side that’s turned away from the viewer. |
| `.back` | Initially rotated 180° so that it becomes visible after the parent rotates. |

Feel free to replace the text or add images inside `.front` and `.back`. Adjust the dimensions, colors, or transition timing to fit your design.
